#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:3
msgid "dm-inlinecrypt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:5
msgid ""
"Device-Mapper's \"inlinecrypt\" target provides transparent encryption of "
"block devices using the inline encryption hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:8
msgid ""
"For a more detailed description of inline encryption, see: https://docs."
"kernel.org/block/inline-encryption.html"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:11
msgid "Parameters::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:16
msgid "<cipher>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:17
msgid "Encryption cipher type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:19
msgid "The cipher specifications format is::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:23
msgid "Examples::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:27
msgid ""
"The cipher type corresponds to the encryption modes supported by inline "
"crypto in the block layer. Currently, only BLK_ENCRYPTION_MODE_AES_256_XTS "
"(i.e. aes-xts-plain64) is supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:31
msgid "<key>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:32
msgid ""
"Key used for encryption. It is encoded either as a hexadecimal number or it "
"can be passed as <key_string> prefixed with single colon character (':') for "
"keys residing in kernel keyring service. You can only use key sizes that are "
"valid for the selected cipher. Note that the size in bytes of a valid key "
"must be in bellow range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:38
msgid "[BLK_CRYPTO_KEY_TYPE_RAW, BLK_CRYPTO_KEY_TYPE_HW_WRAPPED]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:40
msgid "<key_string>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:41
msgid ""
"The kernel keyring key is identified by string in following format: "
"<key_size>:<keyring_type>:<key_description>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:44
msgid "<key_size>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:45
msgid ""
"The encryption key size in bytes. The kernel key payload size must match the "
"value passed in <key_size>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:48
msgid "<keyring_type>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:49
msgid ""
"The type of the key inside the kernel keyring. It can be either 'logon', or "
"'trusted' kernel key type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:52
msgid "<key_description>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:53
msgid ""
"The kernel keyring key description inlinecrypt target should look for when "
"loading key of <keyring_type>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:56
msgid "<iv_offset>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:57
msgid ""
"The IV offset is a sector count that is added to the sector number before "
"creating the IV."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:60
msgid "<device path>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:61
msgid ""
"This is the device that is going to be used as backend and contains the "
"encrypted data.  You can specify it as a path like /dev/xxx or a device "
"number <major>:<minor>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:65
msgid "<offset>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:66
msgid "Starting sector within the device where the encrypted data begins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:68
msgid "<#opt_params>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:69
msgid ""
"Number of optional parameters. If there are no optional parameters, the "
"optional parameters section can be skipped or #opt_params can be zero. "
"Otherwise #opt_params is the number of following arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:73
msgid "Example of optional parameters section:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:74
msgid "keytype:raw allow_discards sector_size:4096 iv_large_sectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:76
msgid "<key_type>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:77
msgid ""
"The type of the key as seen by the block layer, either standard or hardware-"
"wrapped. The string is supplied in the table as <keytype:raw> or <keytype:hw-"
"wrapped>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:81
msgid "allow_discards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:82
msgid ""
"Block discard requests (a.k.a. TRIM) are passed through the inlinecrypt "
"device. The default is to ignore discard requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:85
msgid ""
"WARNING: Assess the specific security risks carefully before enabling this "
"option.  For example, allowing discards on encrypted devices may lead to the "
"leak of information about the ciphertext device (filesystem type, used space "
"etc.) if the discarded blocks can be located easily on the device later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:91
msgid "sector_size:<bytes>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:92
msgid ""
"Use <bytes> as the encryption unit instead of 512 bytes sectors. This option "
"can be in range 512 - 4096 bytes and must be power of two. Virtual device "
"will announce this size as a minimal IO and logical sector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:96
msgid "iv_large_sectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:97
msgid ""
"Use <sector_size>-based sector numbers for IV generation instead of 512-byte "
"sectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:100
msgid ""
"For dm-inlinecrypt, this flag must be specified when <sector_size> is larger "
"than 512 bytes. The legacy 512-byte-based IV behavior is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:104
msgid ""
"When specified, if <sector_size> is 4096 bytes, plain64 IV for the second "
"sector will be 1, and <iv_offset> must be a multiple of <sector_size> (in "
"512-byte units)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:109
msgid "Example scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:110
msgid ""
"Currently, dm-inlinecrypt devices must be set up directly using dmsetup. "
"There is no userspace support yet to integrate dm-inlinecrypt with LUKS or "
"cryptsetup. In particular, cryptsetup currently only supports dm-crypt, and "
"cannot be used to create dm-inlinecrypt mappings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/device-mapper/dm-inlinecrypt.rst:115
msgid ""
"The following examples demonstrate how to create dm-inlinecrypt devices "
"using dmsetup"
msgstr ""
